{
  "an4.160:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 4.160 ",
  "an4.160:0.2": "16. Faculties ",
  "an4.160:0.3": "The Training of a Holy One ",
  "an4.160:1.1": "“Mendicants, a Holy One or a Holy One’s training remain in the world for the welfare and happiness of the people, out of sympathy for the world, for the benefit, welfare, and happiness of gods and humans. ",
  "an4.160:2.1": "And who is a Holy One? ",
  "an4.160:2.2": "It’s when a Realized One arises in the world, perfected, a fully awakened Buddha, accomplished in knowledge and conduct, holy, knower of the world, supreme guide for those fit for training, teacher of gods and humans, awakened, blessed. ",
  "an4.160:2.3": "This is a Holy One. ",
  "an4.160:3.1": "And what is the training of a Holy One? ",
  "an4.160:3.2": "He teaches Dhamma that’s good in the beginning, good in the middle, and good in the end, meaningful and well-phrased. And he reveals a spiritual practice that’s entirely full and pure. ",
  "an4.160:3.3": "This is the training of a Holy One. ",
  "an4.160:3.4": "This is how a Holy One or a Holy One’s training remain in the world for the welfare and happiness of the people, out of sympathy for the world, for the benefit, welfare, and happiness of gods and humans. ",
  "an4.160:4.1": "These four things lead to the decline and disappearance of the true teaching. ",
  "an4.160:4.2": "What four? ",
  "an4.160:4.3": "Firstly, the mendicants memorize discourses that they learned incorrectly, with misplaced words and phrases. ",
  "an4.160:4.